  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: The still water of Verehn's reservoirs has marine
    life like no other. Resistant to all kinds of chemical waste, these organisms
    manage to thrive in small populations despite the myriad diseases they accrue
    just from existing. Fishermen who are without work due to the quarantine have
    begun moving in droves to these reservoirs. But what of the quality of these
    fish? That's a question fishermen don't want to answer. They just enjoy having
    work.
